# User-version upgrade (welcome overlay + guided inquiry + controls tutorial)

The authoritative instructions are the **skill bundle**, not this file:

```
User_version_sims_skills/
  README.md                       ← read first; order of work + gate list
  guided-inquiry/SKILL.md         + references/implementation.md, references/golden-flows.md
  controls-tutorial/SKILL.md      + references/implementation.md
  welcome-overlay/SKILL.md        + references/implementation.md
  tests/                          kernel-diff · layout-probe · canvas-check · browser-smoke
  examples/                       validated builds with all three layers applied
```

This rule exists to record **where output goes** and **what has already gone wrong**, so
neither is rediscovered per sim. Read the bundle for the how.

## WHERE THE OUTPUT GOES — do not write beside the source

User versions never overwrite the production sim. Each course has one destination:

| Course | Source | **Write the user version to** |
|---|---|---|
| **Particle physics** | `Fermi_Particle_physics_sims/Sims_v2_lecture_versions/<sim>.html` | **`Fermi_university_sim_lab_sims/PP_sims/<sim>.html`** |
| Special relativity | `Fermi_SR_simulations/Capacity_SR_sims_v2_engine/shell-versions/<sim>.html` | `Fermi_university_sim_lab_sims/SR_sims/<sim>.html` |
| Classical mechanics | `Fermi_CM_simulations/<sim>.html` | `Fermi_university_sim_lab_sims/CM_sims/<sim>.html` |
| Quantum | `Fermi_QM_simulations/...` | `Fermi_university_sim_lab_sims/QM_sims/<sim>.html` |

Keep the **same filename** as the source. The production sim must end byte-identical —
verify with an md5 before and after.

## ADDITIVE ONLY

Add the three layers; change nothing in the simulation — not physics, drawing code,
controls, readouts or layout, and not even a `const`→`let`. Never remove an element id;
hide what must not show (`display:none`) so `kernel-diff` stays clean.

If a card's answer is already visible in the apparatus and cannot be hidden additively,
**report it and leave it** — prefer reframing that card as a mechanism/inference question.

## NO SPOILERS — the rule that matters most

The welcome hero must not answer any gated inquiry card. Read the deck first, list every
gated card with its correct answer, then design around them.

In the SR/CM fleet **28 of 55 heroes were found leaking a gated answer**, and **nine
asserted in their own code comments that they were safe**. The leaks were almost never
numeric — "it carries no numbers" is not a defence:

- dot spacing ∝ cos(latitude) → showed a deflection vanishing at the equator
- phase advancing across a row of identical clocks → the *envelope* traced the answer
- two rows of marks whose growing gap constructed a velocity difference
- 26 dots on one leg vs 106 on the other → "four times as long in the slow leg"
- the sides of a regular polygon → the order of symmetry, countable
- a card's **wrong** answer drawn, teaching a falsehood

## v2 PP SHELL — traps already verified, handle every time

1. **Retiring Lecture mode un-suppresses things.** `onReset()` runs `for(i) onStep(i)`,
   populating the library/collectible strip with every scripted card's result. Lecture used
   to wipe it; removing Lecture un-wipes it, so a cold boot can display a later card's answer.
   After retiring Lecture, **enumerate everything Lecture was silently suppressing** and
   confirm with a cold boot that no result glyph is on screen before the student acts.
2. **Retire 🎓 Lecture and hide Hide Text (`#ht-ctl`)** — `display:none`, ids preserved.
   An empty Hide-Text registry means touring it would show a control that does nothing, and
   its boot handler reads the `lecture-mode` class being removed.
3. **Reset does not re-arm gates** — the shell's choice handler latches `data-answered`
   forever. Add a re-arm to `__fullReset`: clear `data-answered`/`data-ready`, re-enable every
   `.choice`, drop `.correct/.wrong/.dim`, empty every `.predict-eval`, return to card 1.
   Verify by **clicking** Reset, not by calling the hook.
4. **`data-build` commit latches** — cards that build their own evidence must re-derive from
   `data-answered` inside `onStep` (not only `__giResume`), or the pager shows an answered
   card in its pre-commit state.
5. **`verify.js` counts hidden `.inq-after` text** against the word budget; a card at 80
   visible words can fail the 90-word limit on hidden copy alone.
6. **`.cg-nav` geometry** — the layout probe effectively wants `width:284px` (the grid is a
   fixed `1fr 320px`, so 320 − 2×18) and `right:18px`. Auto width lands ~24–28px off.
7. **Callout placement** — cap the anchor rect at ~200px tall, or a full-column canvas pushes
   the callout to `y=8` onto `#btn-gi`/`#btn-cg`; add an obstacle pass over `#btn-gi`,
   `#btn-cg`, `.cg-nav`.

## HERO BAND

`<canvas id="welcome-fringes">` inside `.welcome-hero`: full viewport width × 140px,
`opacity:.9`, CSS mask fading the outer 22% each side. `.welcome-body{padding:156px 0 0}`
puts the title **below**, so the band is its own space, not a backdrop behind type.

- **Never assume the band's y-position** — it varies by viewport *and* by build (the card is
  vertically centred and its height depends on the subtitle). Measure `getBoundingClientRect()`.
- Size the backing store from that rect at **1:1**; do **not** apply DPR.
- **`ma-perturbation-breakdown.opus-5.html` is a useful structural reference, but its hero is
  wrong** — `<canvas width="1280" height="240">` in a `100vw × 140px` box, stretched
  0.91 × 1.71. Match its structure, never its sizing.
- Watch for a stale anisotropic pre-compensation (`SY = SX*k`, `ctx.scale(1/AR,1)`) when
  adapting existing hero code — four builds carried one and were silently stretching art.
  A squashed diagram falsifies angles. Measure a known-round element off the bitmap.
- Draw **statically** in one pass. `drawHero` is re-run by `animationend`, a timer and two
  MutationObservers, each clearing the canvas — rAF accumulation gets wiped half-built.
- Feather top/bottom with a `destination-out` wipe. Light theme wants proper **dark** ink on
  the near-white ground, not mid-tones. No text or digits on the canvas.

## TOKEN DISCIPLINE

These sims are ~310 KB and **~73% is a single base64 font line**. Never open a sim or an
example whole — `grep -n` for anchors, `sed` narrow ranges, and filter long lines
(`awk 'length < 2000'`). A bare grep on these files can return 200 KB+ from inside the blob.

## GATES

Run all of: the three `scripts/verify.js` (always `--baseline <original>`),
`tests/kernel-diff.mjs --allow-script-edits` (0 canvases changed, 0 ids removed, styles
append-only — its "visible text removed" check *will* fire on replaced card copy: print the
complete list and confirm every chunk is old card copy, never sim UI/readout/legend text),
and `tests/layout-probe.mjs`.

Known tooling gaps: `tests/canvas-check.mjs` hardcodes a QM directory and will `ENOENT` —
measure the backing-store:CSS-box ratio directly instead. `playwright` is not installed, so
`tests/browser-smoke.js` cannot run — substitute a puppeteer-core walk.

Browser-verify in **both themes at 1400×900 and 1024×768**: overlay cold on every boot and
three entry cards reaching three distinct modes; every gate blocking Next **walked forward at
student speed** (not only from a fresh Reset — that is how a cascading gate leak once hid);
commit marking exactly one correct and disabling the rest; Reset re-arming by real click; the
controls sidebar opening empty with every step's glow target visible; plus ≥6 cold boots with
`localStorage` cleared. **Verify the render, not the code** — measure angles and ratios off
the bitmap where they matter.
